# slug: ch23-inline
# source: chapters/ch23.tex:125 (approximate line of \begin{algorithm})
# caption: Greedy cost-guided inlining with a size budget
# label: alg:ch23-inline
# require: call graph G, size budget B, scoring function Score
# ensure: inlined module with updated G
# keywords: INPUT/OUTPUT/REQUIRE/ENSURE/FOR/FORALL/WHILE/IF/ELSE/RETURN

REQUIRE call graph G, size budget B, scoring function Score
ENSURE inlined module with updated G
compute initial size S of each function
build worklist W of eligible direct call sites
WHILE W != {} DO
  remove the site c with the highest Score(c) from W
  IF Score(c) <= 0 THEN
    BREAK
  END IF
  IF inlining c exceeds budget B THEN
    CONTINUE
  END IF
  splice a renamed copy of the callee at c
  run local cleanup: fold, propagate, eliminate dead code
  update sizes S, call graph G, and affected scores
  add newly exposed call sites to W
END WHILE
emit specialized clones for profitable constant keys
redirect matching call sites to the clones

